# demo_device.diff: one fake Pioneer player running INSIDE the app (no runner, no network).
# Upstream: yabb85/controlP commit cad5d5c626516dcbf18719194c92e63f06128d62 (branch dev). App dir src/.
# Used by build.yml input `patches` (git apply --verbose in the fetched repo root, before the spec).
# git apply ignores this text before the first "diff --git" line.
# What it does:
# - Adds src/controlp/pioneer/_fake_pioneer.py, a byte-identical copy of tools/fakes/pioneer.py.
# - scan() starts it on 127.0.0.1 (TCP 8102 + HTTP 18080, daemon threads), then uses its description URL.
# - Everything after that is their real code over loopback sockets: requests, lxml, api.py.
# - Fake traffic is printed as FAKEPIONEER lines (logcat tag python).
# For a real phone (devicelab.yml), where no sidecar can run. Also works on the emulator without a sidecar.
# Do NOT combine with fake_pioneer.diff (same function).
# Regenerate after tools/fakes/pioneer.py changes: copy it to the new file in a pristine checkout of the
# upstream commit, then git diff --no-index (see docs/inspect.md "Driving controlP").

diff --git a/src/controlp/pioneer/_fake_pioneer.py b/src/controlp/pioneer/_fake_pioneer.py
